          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: On Saturday, December 6 at 22:18, a witness observed three red-orange glowing points silently and consistently moving across the sky on a northwest to southeast trajectory. The witness just had time to take three pictures before the phenomenon was obscured by the roof of the building. He then observed a fourth object with the same characteristics moving on the same trajectory. The observation lasted approximately fifteen minutes in total. The noted characteristics (red-orange color, slow and straight movement consistent with a wind at a few degrees) strongly suggest a misidentification with a festive lantern flight (so-called Thai or Chinese lanterns). The time and date (Saturday after 22:00, St. Nicholas Day, a very celebrated holiday in Alsace) are perfectly compatible with this hypothesis. This observation case is a classic misidentification with festive lanterns. This case is classified B as a very probable observation of festive lanterns.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "40cf0d0bf7913be4428edf1bb0f1488e437850241225f0c15fb8a37971363590"
        }
